-- title:
--   Hecke correspondences at two primes commute on divisors
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive integer, let $\ell$ and $\ell'$ be primes and let $q'$ be a prime with $\ell \neq q'$, $\ell' \neq q'$ and $q' \nmid N$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$. For a prime $q$, the field $\mathtt{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,k\,N\,q$ is the intermediate field of $k \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k$ generated by $jqModC\,k$, $jqNModC\,k\,N$, $jqNModC\,k\,q$ and $jqNModC\,k\,(N q)$; it receives the level-$N$ modular function field $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N = k(jqModC\,k, jqNModC\,k\,N)$ by two $k$-algebra maps, the inclusion `heckeAlphaC k N q` and the map `heckeBetaC k N q` induced by the Laurent-series substitution operator `qExpand k q`. Assume that both roofs, at $q = \ell$ and at $q = \ell'$, have principal divisors (every nonzero element $f$ has a finitely supported integer divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ and whose degree is $0$), and assume the predicates `HeckeAlphaCIntegral` and `HeckeBetaCIntegral` at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$, i.e. that all four of these algebra maps are integral. Then for every divisor $D$ on $\mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,N$, the two correspondences — pull back along `heckeAlphaC` followed by push forward along `heckeBetaC`, at $\ell$ and at $\ell'$ respectively — commute when applied to $D$.
--
--   This is the commutativity of the two degeneracy-roof Hecke correspondences of level $N$ at two primes distinct from the residue characteristic, asserted on divisors rather than on divisor classes; the primes $\ell$ and $\ell'$ are allowed to divide $N$ or to coincide. It feeds the construction of Hecke transport and level-prime intertwining data in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development.
